<div class="g-block-width g-max-width-body svelte-rhgw2n"> <p class="g-wrapper_meta g-text-align-left svelte-1p67b3d" style="--g-caption-display:inline;--g-caption-margin-bottom:0;">   <span class="g-credit svelte-1p67b3d">Video by Yuvraj Khanna for The New York Times</span></p> </div></div></figure> </div> <p class="g-text svelte-182b24z">Serenity can be a kind of resistance. The chef Isao Yamada does not preside over this Chinatown kaiseki counter; he goes about his work, calm and intent, affirming that cooking, however rarefied, is a daily practice. Each ingredient is presented like an old friend, welcomed back after the turn of seasons. With each bite, you know when and where you are, and maybe even why.</p> <dl class="bottom svelte-182b24z"><dd class="dd-address svelte-182b24z">16 Elizabeth Street, Chinatown</dd> <dd class="dd-website svelte-182b24z"><a href="https://www.yamadanewyork.com/">yamadanewyork.com</a></dd>
